messages.content:
Build a real-time line chart control for Uno Platform and a page that shows it on a live feed:
- the chart is drawn with SkiaSharp and fills its container;
- a smooth line with a gradient fill under it, a grid with value and time labels, and a badge with the latest value at the line's end;
- the line, the value range and the badge ease toward each new value instead of jumping, and the chart stops redrawing once it settles;
- a live dot with a soft halo marks the latest value at the line's end;
- one colour sets the whole palette, in dark or light;
- a loading state before the first data arrives;
- the page shows one chart in a rounded card, fed by a volatile random walk with a new value every 150 ms.

Stack: Uno Platform single project, SkiaSharp on SKCanvasElement, Material, Toolkit, desktop and WebAssembly.
